Let protocol/meson.build find wayland-scanner when wayland is a subproject.

get_variable(pkgconfig: ...) only reads a pkg-config variable, so it fails when
wayland-scanner comes from the wayland subproject, which provides it as an internal
dependency variable. The positional form reads either, as wlroots already does.
This project builds wayland 1.24 as a subproject because wlroots 0.20 needs it and
the SteamOS 3.8 build root has 1.23.1. No runtime change.

diff --git a/protocol/meson.build b/protocol/meson.build
index c9289f85..5def9d97 100644
--- a/protocol/meson.build
+++ b/protocol/meson.build
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 fs = import('fs')
 
 wayland_scanner_dep = dependency('wayland-scanner', native: true)
-wayland_scanner_path = wayland_scanner_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'wayland_scanner')
+wayland_scanner_path = wayland_scanner_dep.get_variable('wayland_scanner')
 wayland_scanner = find_program(wayland_scanner_path, native: true)
 
 wayland_protos = dependency('wayland-protocols',
